1
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:15,557
( tense sombre music )

2
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:14,783
- [ Woman ] To my daughter , Linda Mary Stevens ,

3
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:18,787
I leave my entire inheritance .

4
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:23,333
All goods , chattles and worldly possessions

5
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:27,587
that comprise the estate of Montclare .

6
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:17,488
- [ Radio Reporter ] Thunderstorms bringing in

7
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:18,948
a cooler change later on today .

8
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:20,033
There 'll be some rain again tonight

9
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:22,076
and tomorrow we can expect yet another fine

10
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:23,453
and warm day .

11
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,622
While we 're talking in the studio today ,

12
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:30,251
( drowned out by gravel and car revving )

13
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:56,402
( zooming )

14
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:58,571
residents in the area or even the tourists

15
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:00,657
that might be listening would like to run over

16
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:02,575
a few of these procedures for us .

17
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:03,576
- [ Man ] Certainly would , Ryan .

18
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:06,246
And needless to say there 's a fire ban on lighting fires

19
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,580
in the open right now .

20
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,708
We should clear all combustible materials

21
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:13,127
from around your home or your caravan even .

22
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:15,380
And all rubbish down at the gathering .

23
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,674
- Easy on the onions , Harry .

24
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:18,758
- [ Harry ] No worries .

25
00:04:20,385 --> 00:04:21,302
- Oy , dad .

26
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:23,429
- [ Harry ] Nico , where you been , huh ?

27
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,555
- [ Nico ] With Linda .

28
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:26,683
- Oh , good day , Linda .

29
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:27,558
- [ Linda ] Hi .

30
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:28,518
- Welcome home .

31
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:29,310
- Thanks .

32
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:33,147
- Nico , get a cup of coffee for Linda , eh ?

33
00:04:33,147 --> 00:04:35,608
- Come , look , you haven 't even eaten your egg there .

34
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:37,944
Come on , Louis , don 't play with your food .

35
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:38,945
Here look , I 'll feed you .

36
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:40,863
- What do you think of the old time , Linda ?

37
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:42,865
Not much changed huh ?

38
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:44,575
- Hardly at all .

39
00:04:44,575 --> 00:04:46,786
- Well there 's a new public toilet .

40
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:49,289
Took them 20 years to get that one up .

41
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:51,291
- Change ?

42
00:04:52,458 --> 00:04:53,293
( banging )

43
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:56,337
- Don 't you look at me like that , young man .

44
00:04:57,463 --> 00:04:58,464
You want me to knock you through

45
00:04:58,464 --> 00:05:00,091
to the middle of next week ?

46
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:01,926
Come closer so I can hit you , Jason .

47
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:05,305
( light music )

48
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,808
Get here and eat up .

49
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,315
- On the house .

50
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,817
- [ Linda ] A test of nerves .

51
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:20,320
- Watch this .

52
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:28,661
- [ Man ] Hey Harry , come on , hurry up .

53
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:30,747
- Two hamburgers coming up .

54
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:31,622
Nico !

55
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:33,875
Nico !

56
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,048
- There we go .

57
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:42,759
And about time too , kid .

58
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:44,635
- I 'm sorry about your mother , Linda .

59
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:50,391
( cashier ringing )

60
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:52,185
She was a good woman , Miss Berry .

61
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:53,644
- Thanks .

62
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:56,773
- [ Harry ] She used to come in here sometimes , you know ?

63
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,066
- My mother ?

64
00:05:58,066 --> 00:05:58,900
- Yeah .

65
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:01,861
Used to sit over in that corner

66
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,071
for a long while .

67
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:05,823
Just looking out of the window as if ,

68
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:08,910
as if something was on her mind , you know .

69
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,788
Nico liked her .

70
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:12,914
He liked her very much .

71
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:16,376
He used to sit with her .

72
00:06:16,376 --> 00:06:17,168
No talking .

73
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:19,379
Just sitting .

74
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:26,386
What you gonna do with that big house now , Linda , huh ?

75
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,974
( birds chirping )

76
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:05,425
( thunder rumbling )

77
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:13,933
- Lance , what are you doing ?

78
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:16,436
- Hmm , watering the flowers .

79
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:17,270
- A bit ?

80
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:20,273
Come and help me take the washing in .

81
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,861
- I think it 's going to rain .

82
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:27,780
( fabrics flapping )

83
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:46,132
Our loves and comforts should increase

84
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:50,303
even as our days do go .

85
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:51,762
- Here , grab this .

86
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,942
( rain pattering )

87
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:09,280
- [ Lance ] Hope it 's a good storm , I like the rain .

88
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:20,666
( light music )

89
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:48,945
- [ Woman ] Now mother and father have gone ,

90
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,948
we have the problem of maintaining Montclare .

91
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:54,116
We 're determined not to sell it .

92
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:56,035
I suggested to Rita that we might turn it

93
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:58,663
into a nursing home and she seemed to like the idea .

94
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:01,832
25th of August , 1950 .

95
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:11,384
( chiming )

96
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:45,376
( thunder rumbling )

97
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:47,837
( cat mewing )

98
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,453
( clanging )

99
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:37,928
- Shit .

100
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:46,812
( lightning clapping )

101
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:49,065
- Can I give you a hand ?

102
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:50,149
- Oh , Connie .

103
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,904
I can 't close it .

104
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,906
We 'll have to get it repaired .

105
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,658
- You should be careful .

106
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,950
- What 's that ?

107
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:00,951
- The wires .

108
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,084
- Let 's get out of here .

109
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:16,842
- Do you think it 's a good idea moving

110
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,844
your mother 's belongings right now ?

111
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,429
- It 's got to be done sometime .

112
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:22,098
- The old people are a little sensitive .

113
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,849
It 's best when they 're all asleep .

114
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:25,685
- Whose room is this ?

115
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,311
- The new arrival .

116
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:28,854
- What 's she talking about ?

117
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,856
- Somebody 's gotta do the

118
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,108
flowers . - Mrs. Ryan .

119
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,694
Her nephew 's bringing her up tonight .

120
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:35,736
- We 've already discussed this .

121
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,988
I don 't want to take any more people .

122
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:38,948
- We need the money .

123
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,783
- Yes I know , but one more person

124
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,535
isn 't going to make any difference .

125
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,538
It 's just all too much .

126
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:47,998
- Oh no , it 's just maintenance .

127
00:11:47,998 --> 00:11:49,125
And the old for their mind ,

128
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:50,292
they still love it here .

129
00:11:51,877 --> 00:11:54,130
- You 're a great optimist , Connie .

130
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,715
I better see Mr. Collins .

131
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:02,388
( coughing )

132
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:04,014
Cold night , Mr. Collins .

133
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,726
How are your eyes ?

134
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,185
Let 's have a look .

135
00:12:08,185 --> 00:12:09,145
Head back .

136
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:11,230
Look at the ceiling .

137
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:17,737
( thunder rumbling )

138
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:39,592
( booming )

139
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:43,554
- Good god .

140
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:13,334
- You 'll get soaked !

141
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:18,339
I 'll get them .

142
00:13:19,298 --> 00:13:21,509
Come on , let 's get you inside .

143
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:22,843
- They 're crazy .

144
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,264
- You should have gone to the front entrance .

145
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,974
- We got lost .

146
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:31,352
The lightning nearly got us .

147
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:33,145
- You should be in bed .

148
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:34,146
- Oh , rubbish .

149
00:13:34,146 --> 00:13:35,231
And miss all the fun ?

150
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:38,984
- Damn , door 's locked .

151
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:41,237
( knocking )

152
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:52,373
- Look , you 'll have to walk .

153
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:02,132
- I was locked out of the barracks .

154
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:04,134
It was teeming with rain just like this .

155
00:14:04,134 --> 00:14:05,386
- [ Linda ] Cathy !

156
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:07,012
- [ Lance ] Enemy shell started exploding

157
00:14:07,012 --> 00:14:08,472
all over the bloody camp .

158
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:09,682
( knocking )

159
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,350
- What happened ?

160
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:12,601
- The door slammed ?

161
00:14:12,601 --> 00:14:14,144
- Didn 't you slip the lock ?

162
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,314
I 'm sorry Mr. Ryan .

163
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,441
You must be tired after your long journey .

164
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:22,862
This is Linda , Mr. Cooney .

165
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,030
Mrs. Ryan and Mr. Ryan .

166
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:25,865
- Kelvin .

167
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,869
- Wasn 't your Aunt happy in the last house ?

168
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:31,620
- They weren 't happy .

169
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,459
- Then I got back and I put it like anyone here ,

170
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:39,503
thunder was coming and explosions

171
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,171
all over the bloody place .

172
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:42,506
I didn 't know what the hell to do .

173
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:45,050
And you know , it doesn 't often rain in North Africa

174
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:47,219
but my god , when it does it does come down

175
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:48,929
in buckets and lumps .

176
00:14:48,929 --> 00:14:50,180
- Good heavens .

177
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:53,058
- I 'll take care of Mrs. Ryan .

178
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:54,143
- Come on Lance .

179
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:55,019
- You better stay the night , Mr. Ryan .

180
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,562
We 've got a spare room upstairs .

181
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:58,772
- Come on .

182
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:00,190
- Well anyhow , there I was .

183
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,650
I 'd locked out of the barracks .

184
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:03,235
I couldn 't get in no matter how much I yelled .

185
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:04,904
- Bags with Cynthia .

186
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:07,072
- Is this the new one ?

187
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:07,907
- Yes .

188
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,366
- If we get any more , we 'd have to stick them

189
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:10,326
up the chimney .

190
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:11,577
- Anyhow , what can I do ?

191
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:12,494
I couldn 't get into the barracks .

192
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:14,163
I said the only thing to do is walk

193
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:15,581
back to the latrine .

194
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:17,207
While I was on the way there , halfway there

195
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:21,211
then whoah , a whacking shell just blew the dunny sky high .

196
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:28,427
( rain pattering )

197
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:38,103
- [ Woman ] Lance has been like a father to Linda .

198
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:40,105
He drove with me into town today to buy Linda

199
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:42,775
a birthday present , a red ball .

200
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:45,194
Then in his usual absent minded way

201
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,612
forgot to pay Mr. Foley .

202
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:49,239
I discreetly settled the bill .

203
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:51,200
Thursday .

204
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:54,662
Someone was wandering around the house last night .

205
00:15:55,537 --> 00:15:58,248
I didn 't sleep .

206
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:00,501
( thunder rumbling )

207
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:03,003
( tense music )

208
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,605
( light music )

209
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:45,189
( birds chirping )

210
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:59,369
( water splashing )

211
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:20,432
( singing in foreign language )

212
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:21,558
- It 's from my niece .

213
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:23,727
Shelly .

214
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:25,104
- What is it ?

215
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,522
- I have no idea .

216
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:34,279
- Hey , turn that thing off .

217
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,614
You make the telly go all fuzzy .

218
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:37,991
All the fuss about ,

219
00:18:37,991 --> 00:18:40,119
never stops cleaning , that woman .

220
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:40,953
- Morning .

221
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:43,789
Mrs. Collins and Lance not here yet .

222
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:45,707
- Lance usually waits till the last one 's finished .

223
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:47,417
Thinks he gets better service that way

224
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:48,961
even though the food gets cold .

225
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:52,798
- We 'll have to do something about that fallen tree .

226
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:53,924
- I 've organised it .

227
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:54,758
We 'll manage .

228
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:03,267
- I might go into town and get you some oranges .

229
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,393
Would you like some sherry ?

230
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:07,146
I 'll get you some sherry .

231
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,313
- [ Mrs. Ryan ] The dry one ?

232
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:09,982
- [ Kelvin ] The dry one .

233
00:19:09,982 --> 00:19:14,486
Look I think this place is gonna do you a lot of good .

234
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:28,458
( ominous music )

235
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:03,512
( honking )

236
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:29,288
( fly buzzing )

237
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:46,638
( whistle blowing )

238
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:50,434
( woman shouting in distance )

239
00:21:55,897 --> 00:21:58,317
( whistling )

240
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,071
- How you been ?

241
00:22:04,114 --> 00:22:04,948
- Okay .

242
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:08,785
- You look great .

243
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:12,497
- Where 's your car ?

244
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:13,623
- I lost my licence .

245
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:17,502
( light music )

246
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:24,801
Here I come !

247
00:22:24,801 --> 00:22:25,635
Woo !

248
00:22:52,245 --> 00:22:53,622
- Yuck .

249
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:55,082
This water stinks .

250
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:57,918
I hate dead flowers .

251
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:01,380
You know I didn 't miss her at first .

252
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:04,049
She had secrets .

253
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:06,635
Here .

254
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:07,427
- Oh , thank you .

255
00:23:08,553 --> 00:23:09,805
- I suppose you think I 'm like her .

256
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:10,806
- Yup .

257
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:11,807
- Unreliable .

258
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:12,933
- Mhmm .

259
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:14,184
- Unpredictable .

260
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:15,560
- Uh-huh .

261
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,020
- Crazy .

262
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:17,854
- Oh yes .

263
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:20,399
- Good .

264
00:23:21,566 --> 00:23:22,734
- You haven 't changed .

265
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:24,403
- What has ?

266
00:23:24,403 --> 00:23:25,404
- Plenty .

267
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:26,405
What do you wanna know ?

268
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:27,572
- Nothing .

269
00:23:27,572 --> 00:23:29,699
- Not even that Tom 's got a new stud phone ?

270
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:31,993
Lucy Parker , the fat girl ?

271
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:32,953
- God , no .

272
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:34,204
- None in New Guinea .

273
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:36,665
- There 's a place for her .

274
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:37,916
- Doreen Lauren .

275
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:40,252
- No . ( giggling )

276
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,086
( mumbling )

277
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:41,920
